# 2. DESIGN DIRECTION

## 2.1 Product experience

MOMENT should feel like a modern social discovery and micro-entertainment platform.

The interface should communicate:

- Discovery.
- Spontaneity.
- Participation.
- Entertainment.
- Human connection.
- Community activity.

The application must not visually or functionally become a conventional follower-centric social network.

The main experience should encourage users to discover something interesting, participate, and continue exploring without unnecessary complexity.

## 2.2 Visual design principles

The implementation should use:

- Clear visual hierarchy.
- Readable typography.
- Consistent spacing.
- Well-defined content cards.
- Distinct primary and secondary actions.
- Subtle and purposeful motion.
- Consistent iconography.
- Appropriate contrast.
- Clean, uncluttered layouts.
- Predictable navigation.

Avoid:

- Excessive gradients.
- Excessive shadows.
- Unnecessary animations.
- Overloaded dashboards.
- Excessively rounded components used inconsistently.
- Tiny interactive targets.
- Unnecessary confirmation dialogs.
- Uncontrolled visual differences between pages.

## 2.3 Brand and design decisions requiring approval

The following values must not be treated as approved brand decisions unless confirmed by the existing project or product owner:

| Design decision | Status |
|---|---|
| Official brand logo | Inspect existing assets |
| Primary brand color | Approval required |
| Secondary brand color | Approval required |
| Accent colors | Approval required |
| Typography family | Approval required |
| Official icon style | Inspect existing implementation |
| Border radius system | Proposed |
| Shadow system | Proposed |
| Animation language | Proposed |
| Dark mode | Product decision required |
| Light mode | Product decision required |
