# 11. PERFORMANCE AND VISUAL STABILITY

## 11.1 Rendering

- Avoid unnecessary client-side rendering.
- Use server components where appropriate.
- Keep client components focused on genuine interactivity.
- Avoid loading large libraries unnecessarily.
- Reuse existing optimized assets.

## 11.2 Images and media

- Use appropriate image dimensions.
- Avoid unnecessary image downloads.
- Use responsive image loading.
- Provide meaningful alternative text where appropriate.
- Prevent large image elements from causing layout shifts.

## 11.3 Loading behavior

- Avoid blocking the entire page for independent content requests.
- Use component-level loading states.
- Avoid repeated network requests caused by incorrect component lifecycle behavior.
- Prevent duplicate pagination requests.

## 11.4 Visual stability

The implementation should be tested for:

- Cumulative Layout Shift.
- Unexpected component resizing.
- Font loading shifts.
- Image loading shifts.
- Navigation movement.
- Mobile viewport changes.

Performance targets must be measured against the actual deployed application and approved performance requirements. Do not claim compliance without measurements.

