# 19. NON-NEGOTIABLE IMPLEMENTATION RULES

The coding agent MUST:

1. Read the Master PRD and Database Specification before implementation.
2. Audit the existing repository before changing UI architecture.
3. Preserve existing working functionality unless a documented change is approved.
4. Reuse existing components where appropriate.
5. Use the approved design system consistently.
6. Keep components maintainable and appropriately scoped.
7. Implement every required state for each major screen.
8. Ensure all visible controls perform their intended actions.
9. Connect interfaces to real backend functionality.
10. Enforce authorization through the backend.
11. Preserve anonymous-post privacy.
12. Prevent location information from being unnecessarily exposed.
13. Test actual mobile behavior.
14. Test keyboard and accessibility behavior.
15. Avoid unnecessary dependencies.
16. Avoid duplicated UI logic.
17. Avoid hardcoded fake data in production interfaces.
18. Avoid placeholder buttons and fake interactions.
19. Avoid unnecessary animations and visual distractions.
20. Record all deviations and unresolved decisions.

The coding agent MUST NOT:

- Invent new MVP features.
- Add direct messaging.
- Add followers or following systems.
- Add live streaming.
- Add virtual currencies or cash rewards.
- Add virtual pets or collectible economies.
- Add unapproved AI recommendation features.
- Add unsupported game modes.
- Add unapproved monetization interfaces.
- Change the approved brand identity without approval.
- Replace the existing UI architecture without justification.
- Remove existing routes without impact analysis.
- Hide backend errors by pretending actions succeeded.
- Use client-side authorization as a security boundary.
- Introduce fake content to make screens look complete.

